        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for EX1-040 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "The attack continues, but the turn doesn't switch over yet.   If the memory gauge is still at 1 or more on your opponent’s side after the attack has ended and all effects triggered by it have been activated, only then does the turn end.",
        "question": "When digivolving with this card's [When Attacking] effect, paying the digivolution cost moves the memory gauge to 1 or more on my opponent’s side. What happens to the attack?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, the time to trigger [When Attacking] effects has already passed, so the effect doesn't activate.",
        "question": "I attack with [EX1-035 Kabuterimon] and digivolve into this card with its [When Attacking] effect. Can I then digivolve again during the same attack with this card's [When Digivolving] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. The effect reads, “This Digimon can digivolve,” so you can choose not to.",
        "question": "If I have a card in hand with [Insectoid] or [Ancient Insect] in its traits, does this card’s [When Attacking] effect force me to digivolve when attacking?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can’t ignore its digivolution requirements.",
        "question": "When digivolving into a Digimon card with [Insectoid] or [Ancient Insect] in its traits in my hand with this Digimon's [When Attacking] effect, can I ignore that card's digivolution requirements?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
